 ### Breaking Changes
 
+- **An access token's revoke records why: `revoke(id, userId, at, reason)` on `AccessTokenService` and `AccessTokenStore`.** `reason` is a
+  string of at most 200 characters, or `null`, stored in the new nullable `auth_access_tokens.revoked_reason` column and read back as
+  `AuthAccessToken.revokedReason`. **Migration:** run `forge db migrate compose` after upgrading — it adds `revoked_reason` in place, with no
+  backfill — and apply it before you deploy. Pass a reason, or `null`, at every `revoke` call; a store of your own writes the column and reads
+  it back. Regenerate the row types with `forge db types`.
 - **Every forge lint message opens with its rule id as `[rule-id] `, and names no corpus file.** A message read
   `<detail> (<id> — <corpus path>)`; it now reads `[<id>] <detail>`, and the 9 rules that reported without an id carry one too, among them
   `[forge-sql-in-loop]` and `[forge-type-import-separation]`. No lint message cites a document section (`DOC.md §N`) any more. Internally each
